course: dictionary
lesson: 9018
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it. «Skittles» can mean a game, the pins used in that game, or a brand of sweets. The clues in the sentence tell you which one the writer means.
explain: «No single food has everything, so eating only pasta like Jade in Belfast misses whole groups, and «eat the rainbow» means peppers, carrots, berries and spinach, not Skittles.» The words food and eat are the clues. Skittles here means the sweets, and the capital S shows it is a name.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If you put "the game" in place of Skittles, the sentence about eating food stops making sense, so that meaning is wrong. Checking like this is the quickest way to be sure.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is being used.
fact: «Skittles» can mean a game, the wooden or plastic pins in the game, or a brand of sweets.
fact: A skittle is one pin. Skittles is the plural, meaning more than one pin, and it is also the name of the game.
fact: The game of skittles is like bowling: you roll a ball to knock down the pins.
fact: Skittles with a capital S is a name: a brand of small, fruity, colourful chewy sweets.
exercise: «In PE, the children played skittles with a ball and plastic pins.» What does skittles mean here? | A wooden table in the hall | A brand of fruity chewy sweets | A bag of food for a rainbow | *A game where you roll a ball to knock down pins
exercise: Maths problem: «10 skittles, 7 knocked down, how many standing?» What does skittles mean in this sum? | Sweets you can eat | The game itself, played with a ball | A kind of ball | *The pins that get knocked down
exercise: «She bought a bag of Skittles after school.» What does Skittles mean here? | *A brand of small, fruity, colourful chewy sweets | A rainbow of peppers and carrots | Wooden pins for knocking down | A game played in the hall
test: Which sentence uses skittles to mean the pins? | *Jade rolled the ball and knocked down all ten skittles | Ali ate three Skittles at lunch | Maya got a bag of Skittles for her birthday
test: Nadia says skittles means only the game. Why is she wrong about «eat the rainbow... not Skittles»? | Because the word skittles has no meaning at all | Because the sentence is about PE, so it means the game | *Because the sentence is about food, so Skittles must mean the sweets
exam: In «eat the rainbow means peppers, carrots, berries and spinach, not Skittles», which clue shows Skittles means sweets? | The word rainbow, which is a game | The word spinach, which is a pin | The word Skittles is written with a capital S | *The words food and eat, which link to sweets as something you eat
